<title>SOUTH AFRICA: FNB sees solid improvement in earnings.</title>
<headline>FNB sees solid improvement in earnings.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>First National Bank Holdings Ltd said on Wednesday it expected a solid improvement in headline earnings for its full financial year.  </p>
<p>&quot;The group is also confident that a solid improvement in headline earnings will be achieved for the full financial year,&quot; managing director Viv Bartlett said in a statement accompanying half-year results.  </p>
<p>After tax profit increased by 27.9 percent to 555.8 million rand in the six months to March 31, 1997 from the previous 434.7 million.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
</text>
